    "src": "§01 world: information moves through people and paper; §03 Fixer is the face witnesses remember; §04 Talker facts (saw Fixer's face); §05 witness 13 m; §08 café owner tips needs",
    "proposed": true,
    "reason": "From DF's rumour rule (a fact exists only for those who saw it or were told) and Adams 2017 (identity stored per observer as alias, name or face). Only face is in play: the Talker's facts are a face, a car, a place-time and (from a captured operative only, brief 018 §3) a turned contact, and §05 investigators hop by place and time, not by name. needsKnown makes §08's tip rule checkable from the cast: a keeper knows the need of each workmate and of each person with a regular tie into their unit, so a turned keeper saves the Listen (42 s) on each. How a fact spreads at runtime (told, along which ties, how fast) is Keel's rule, not this file's."
  },
  "talker": {
    "when": "questioned",
    "test": { "left": ["fear", "resentment"], "op": ">", "right": ["bravery", "loyalty"] },
    "deterministic": true,
    "gives": "known-facts",
    "facts": ["fixer-face", "enforcer-face", "cell-car", "place-time", "cell-face", "contact"],
    "src": "§04 talker [S]: questioned, a person gives up known facts if fear + resentment > bravery + loyalty (deterministic). Each fact, who holds it, and the lead it makes (§05 output: every fact given is a lead). fixer-face: saw the Fixer's face (§03 the face witnesses remember); the lead is the Fixer, known by face. enforcer-face: saw the Enforcer's face (Sky 2026-10-16 D3, brief 013: a witness of a takedown, or a victim who saw him coming); the lead is the Enforcer, known by face. cell-car: knows the cell's car (rode in it; brief 018 §3 and Sky 2026-10-18 answer 5: security that sees the car leave gives it to the investigation, and the car is then known, hunted next mission until the cell answers it, e.g. a new car through a contact; the engine records the fact, the campaign side waits for a campaign layer); the lead is the car. place-time: saw where and when; the lead is that place and time. cell-face:<op> (brief 018 §3): an operative's face, one fact per operative of the cell; only a cell member holds it, so only a captured operative gives it, and gives every operative's; it generalises fixer-face and enforcer-face, which stay the witnesses' facts (cell-face:fixer is the face fixer-face names, cell-face:enforcer the one enforcer-face names); the lead is that operative, known by face. contact:<person> (brief 018 §3): a contact the cell has turned, by person id, one fact per turned contact; only a cell member holds it, so only a captured operative gives it, and gives every one; the lead sends the investigators to that person next mission, where that person's own Talker test applies (§02 the city investigates backward, link by link). A captive who talks gives every fact they hold at once (cell-face for every operative, cell-car, place-time for the mission, contact for every turned contact), and for good",
    "lie": {
      "when": { "talker": false, "helped": true, "braveryAtLeast": 1 },
      "gives": { "hero": "false-lead", "otherwise": "nothing" },
      "src": "§04 brave helped contact lies → nothing or false lead; §05 Hero campaign: brave locals give false leads",
